WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.720
891,348 british columbians have already voted ahead of Saturday's election. This is vancouver

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:14.840
Daily, episode 31. I'm Mira, the Nerranetwork's AI host. I don't live in vancouver. After the

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:20.620
count, a surrey murder verdict, a langley assault investigation, then healthcare strain, metro

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:26.140
reform, getting around, and the case on both sides of grocery prices. Elections B.C. took

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:32.320
those ballots over six days, October 16th through the 21st, and they are about 24% of registered

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:41.060
voters. The Vancouver Sun sets that against 1 million, 1,331 advance votes in 2024, about 28%

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:47.680
of the list. CBC describes the advance total as down 11% from that year. David Black, a political

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:52.880
science professor at Royal Rhodes University, told the Sun that an early count does not reliably

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:57.980
predict who shows up on Election Day. He pointed to a large undecided block and to fatigue

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:00.960
from a snap election called in the middle of a municipal campaign.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:06.600
City News reports elections BC will count Saturday's Election Day ballots by hand. Black

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:10.900
said the advance ballots are already tabulated electronically, so they are likely out

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:12.000
before that hand count.

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:17.460
Turnout Rose and Surrey Serpentine River and in Vancouver, Kulchena, where one BC leader

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:23.320
Dallas Brodie is running and fell across most of Surrey and Vancouver, 22% versus 24

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:26.440
in Surrey, 22 versus 27 in Vancouver.

00:01:27.634 --> 00:01:32.094
ABC Court has convicted Adam Mann of second-degree murder in the killing of Surrey resident

00:01:32.094 --> 00:01:32.854
Torrey Dunn.

00:01:33.454 --> 00:01:36.674
CBC reports the killing happened in a home invasion two years ago.

00:01:37.134 --> 00:01:42.814
Global news reports Dunn was 30 and that she was stabbed four times, one wound 18 centimeters

00:01:42.814 --> 00:01:46.774
into her abdomen, killed her, and two wounds on her hands were defensive.

00:01:47.965 --> 00:01:52.585
Langley, RCMP, are investigating an assault on a driving instructor in a church parking lot.

00:01:53.045 --> 00:01:58.245
Global news reports officers were called to the 4,800 block of 207th Street at about

00:01:58.245 --> 00:02:01.025
nine in the morning on Wednesday, and the lot was empty.

00:02:01.565 --> 00:02:05.345
Corporal Mansour Sahak said a woman was arrested at the scene, then released.

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:08.725
She has not been charged, and she is expected to appear in court.

00:02:09.325 --> 00:02:13.565
Video online appears to show a woman hitting the instructor and saying, go back to your

00:02:13.565 --> 00:02:13.885
country.

00:02:13.885 --> 00:02:19.085
The driving school said it condemns the racism and the aggression in that video, and RCMP

00:02:19.085 --> 00:02:20.905
want witnesses to call investigators.

00:02:22.136 --> 00:02:27.436
Dr. Kevin McLeod, an internal medicine specialist at Lionsgate Hospital, says he is hit a breaking

00:02:27.436 --> 00:02:29.576
point and is seriously considering resigning.

00:02:30.176 --> 00:02:34.416
Global news reports he posted Thursday that a specialist can sold on a complex patient

00:02:34.416 --> 00:02:36.036
in 20 minutes is not safe.

00:02:36.456 --> 00:02:39.836
If he takes longer, he wrote, urgent care waits in the pile grows.

00:02:40.336 --> 00:02:43.396
He said this week has been especially hard on him and on his family.

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:49.556
On a typical call day, he might see 20 to 22 new complex patients plus 35 to 50 people

00:02:49.556 --> 00:02:50.236
in an office.

00:02:50.736 --> 00:02:55.076
What tipped it, he said, was special calling to send patients over because that hospital

00:02:55.076 --> 00:02:56.536
has no physician capacity.

00:02:57.136 --> 00:03:02.016
At Pentectin Regional Hospital, three neurologists have resigned their hospital privileges, and

00:03:02.016 --> 00:03:04.176
patients who need that care could see less of it.

00:03:04.656 --> 00:03:06.796
Interior health brought in the change last month.

00:03:07.216 --> 00:03:10.196
Neurologists must cover on call across the whole health region.

00:03:10.196 --> 00:03:15.876
Dr. Adam Thompson, president of Doctors of BC, said losing doctors from any facility

00:03:15.876 --> 00:03:17.036
is always a concern.

00:03:17.456 --> 00:03:21.276
He said the rule would substantially raise the workload with no extra support in their

00:03:21.276 --> 00:03:23.756
communities, and neurologists are already scarce.

00:03:24.296 --> 00:03:28.296
There is a tipping point, he said, where those cases cannot all be juggled at once.

00:03:28.816 --> 00:03:32.336
McLeod wants the next government to hold highly paid administrators to account.

00:03:32.816 --> 00:03:36.856
He said those admin ranks have grown sharply, and he would not argue the system runs

00:03:36.856 --> 00:03:38.016
more efficiently for it.

00:03:38.016 --> 00:03:43.296
BC NDP leader David E.B. promised to write minimum nurse to patient ratios into law,

00:03:43.576 --> 00:03:46.516
so health authorities and hospital managers would know the direction.

00:03:47.216 --> 00:03:52.336
Adrian Gear, president of the BC Nurses Union, said that legislation could lock in progress

00:03:52.336 --> 00:03:55.336
already made and give patients and nurses more certainty.

00:03:55.896 --> 00:04:00.676
She said it could also back a planned spread of ratios into emergency departments, operating

00:04:00.676 --> 00:04:05.336
rooms, long-term care, assisted living, and community care outside hospitals.

00:04:05.336 --> 00:04:11.056
rules. Safe staffing, she said, has to outlast party politics, whichever party forms government.

00:04:12.059 --> 00:04:16.939
New Westminster Mayor-elect Daniel Fontaine wants a five-point accountability charter in

00:04:16.939 --> 00:04:22.459
front of Metro Vancouver. The Vancouver Sun reports 14 of 21 municipalities elected new

00:04:22.459 --> 00:04:28.359
mayors on October 17th. West Vancouver's mayor-elect Kirk LaPont and White Rock's Chris

00:04:28.359 --> 00:04:32.739
Shields have signed the charter with him. It would pay mayors nothing extra for Metro

00:04:32.739 --> 00:04:37.399
board in committee work, and it calls for a full public review of cost overruns at the

00:04:37.399 --> 00:04:38.759
North Shore Wastewater Plant.

00:04:39.219 --> 00:04:44.019
It also asks for a Smaller Mayor's Council, an auditor general for Metro and its cities,

00:04:44.479 --> 00:04:46.739
and an independent review of critical services.

00:04:47.359 --> 00:04:52.919
Fontaine said Metro has 41 directors and has drifted into housing, parks, and its own investment

00:04:52.919 --> 00:04:53.219
arm.

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:55.159
He does not want Metro abolished.

00:04:55.479 --> 00:04:59.539
He wants it reviewed, and he will bring the charter only if new Westminster Council votes

00:04:59.539 --> 00:05:00.379
him onto the board.

00:05:00.379 --> 00:05:05.639
La Pointe said the region needs a smaller mandate or a directly elected board, plus oversight

00:05:05.639 --> 00:05:06.779
and more transparency.

00:05:07.459 --> 00:05:09.939
Coquitlam mayor-elect Craig Hodge has not signed.

00:05:10.339 --> 00:05:14.819
He told the Sun he supports the reforms that some are already understudy and that the

00:05:14.819 --> 00:05:16.059
public has lost confidence.

