00:07:41.917 --> 00:07:47.537
On grocery prices, the case on both sides is a campaign argument, not a law yet, and voting

00:07:47.537 --> 00:07:48.237
end Saturday.

00:07:48.237 --> 00:07:52.877
The Vancouver Sun reports the NDP and the Greens want the bill at the till to fall.

00:07:53.197 --> 00:07:57.397
The Conservatives say cut taxes instead, so people have more money for food.

00:07:57.957 --> 00:08:03.617
NDP leader David Eby wants a cap on the markup for milk, eggs, cheese, butter, and poultry.

00:08:04.117 --> 00:08:05.197
Aimed at corporate retailers.

00:08:05.677 --> 00:08:11.237
He named Loblaws, Save On Foods, Walmart, Costco, and Sobes, which runs Safeway.

00:08:11.677 --> 00:08:16.977
The Greens would build government-owned grocery stores, 20 to start, with a $100 million investment.

00:08:16.977 --> 00:08:22.297
Those stores would buy local and sell a basket of core goods 30% under market prices.

00:08:23.077 --> 00:08:27.217
Chris Bodner, an assistant professor of agriculture at the University of the Fraser Valley,

00:08:27.517 --> 00:08:32.237
says milk is often a loss leader, priced thin or even at a loss to get people in the door.

00:08:32.797 --> 00:08:36.537
A cap gets attention, he said, and it does not fix what made food expensive.

00:08:37.017 --> 00:08:42.577
Climate, conflicts that raise fertilizer and fuel, and whether BC has the land and water to grow more.

00:08:42.577 --> 00:08:47.257
The Sun cites a Harvard Business School study that found a small temporary break on

00:08:47.257 --> 00:08:50.057
caped items, then higher prices on everything else.

00:08:50.497 --> 00:08:55.157
It also says the International Monetary Fund warns that broad grocery controls send the

00:08:55.157 --> 00:08:59.417
wrong signals and can disrupt supply, and that cash transfers are the better tool.

00:09:00.037 --> 00:09:06.377
Hungary has caped staple prices since 2022, and in 2025 caped retail profit at 10% on

00:09:06.377 --> 00:09:07.857
more than 30 essential foods.

00:09:07.857 --> 00:09:13.217
France, in 2023, negotiated a freeze with the big chains instead of passing a law.

00:09:13.837 --> 00:09:18.717
Tamara Soma, an associate professor at Simon Fraser University, says public stores would

00:09:18.717 --> 00:09:20.477
give shoppers and farmers another buyer.

00:09:20.957 --> 00:09:27.437
She points to about 240 US military commissaries, where shoppers save about 25% on average, and

00:09:27.437 --> 00:09:30.677
to Mexico's subsidized stores selling staples under the market price.

00:09:31.237 --> 00:09:36.537
The five main grocers in BC, she said, sometimes will not take produce that looks a bit off, and

00:09:36.537 --> 00:09:37.417
And a public store could.

00:09:37.957 --> 00:09:40.777
The sun notes those public stores come with an ongoing cost.

